       <h3>Light Up / Illuminate</h3>
       <p>To <strong>light up</strong> or <strong>illuminate</strong> a cell means that at least one bulb's line of sight reaches it. When you place a bulb, it illuminates every white cell in its row and column until blocked by a wall. The win condition of every <a href="/akari/light-up-puzzle/">light up puzzle</a> requires that all white cells are illuminated simultaneously. Cells that are not reached by any bulb remain "dark" and indicate that the puzzle is not yet solved.</p>
 
       <h3>X Mark</h3>
-      <p>An <strong>X mark</strong> is a player-placed annotation on a white cell to indicate that no bulb should go there. X marks are not part of the official Akari rules — they are a solving aid. Most online Akari implementations, including GridPaw, let you place X marks by right-clicking or long-pressing a cell. Using X marks helps you track elimination logic and avoid accidentally placing bulbs in impossible positions. See our <a href="/akari/how-to-play/">how to play guide</a> for more on using X marks effectively.</p>
