       <h2>Solving Technique Terms</h2>
 
       <h3>Elimination</h3>
-      <p><strong>Elimination</strong> is the process of ruling out impossible bulb placements based on logical deduction. When you determine that a cell cannot contain a bulb — because it would violate a number constraint, create a bulb conflict, or leave another cell permanently dark — you eliminate it. Elimination is the bread and butter of Akari solving: every step forward comes from either placing a bulb or eliminating a position. Advanced solvers use systematic elimination chains to crack hard puzzles. We will cover elimination strategies in detail in our upcoming <a href="/akari/tips/">tips and strategies guide</a>.</p>
