       <h2>Read Every Number Cell Before You Place Anything</h2>
-      <p>The single biggest beginner mistake in Akari is placing bulbs reactively — spotting an obvious one and clicking, then hunting for the next. Instead, do a full sweep of the grid first and read <em>every</em> number. A <a href="#number-0">number 0 cell</a> instantly tells you four cells are dead. A <a href="#number-4">number 4 cell</a> hands you four bulbs. Those two reads alone often account for a third of a puzzle's bulbs, and they cost you nothing but a single pass with your eyes.</p>
